  ## 4. Service-layer method(s): every validation check and side-effect, in order

  **File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`

  The controller calls `saveOwner(owner, sharesHousehold)`. The one-arg overload simply delegates with `false` (lines 263-267). The real logic (lines 277-304):

  ```java
  @Override
  @Transactional
  public void saveOwner(Owner owner, boolean sharesHousehold) throws DataAccessException {
      boolean isCreate = owner.isNew();                               // (1)
      assertIdentityIsUnique(owner);                                  // (2) may throw DuplicateIdentityException
      if (owner.isNew()) {
          assertCityHasCapacity(owner);                              // (3) may throw CityAtCapacityException
      }
      if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
          owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());                // (4) default reg date
      }
      owner.setRegistrationDate(rollToBusinessDay(owner.getRegistrationDate())); // (5) weekend→Monday
      if (owner.isNew()) {
          assertDailyRegistrationLimit(owner);                       // (6) may throw DailyRegistrationLimitException
          owner.setBulkSignupWarning(computeBulkSignupWarning(owner)); // (7) set warning flag
      }
      if (owner.isNew() && owner.getCustomerCode() == null) {
          owner.setCustomerCode(generateCustomerCode(owner));       // (8) assign customer code
      }
      if (owner.isNew() && owner.getNamesakeCount() == null) {
          owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner));            // (9) assign namesake count
      }
      ownerRepository.save(owner);                                   // (10) PERSIST
      if (isCreate) {
          AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}",   // (11) audit log
              owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());
      }
  }
  ```

  Note the `sharesHousehold` flag is now a documented **no-op** (lines 269-276).

  Exact order of operations for a create (owner.isNew() == true):

  1. **Capture isCreate** = `owner.isNew()` (true since id is null for a mapped new owner).
  2. **Duplicate-identity check** — `assertIdentityIsUnique(owner)` (lines 365-378). Normalizes the owner's telephone; if null, returns (skips). Otherwise loads ALL owners (`ownerRepository.findAll()`), excludes self by id, normalizes each existing telephone, and if any equals the new normalized telephone, throws `DuplicateIdentityException(identityKey)`. (Effectively a normalized-telephone uniqueness check.)
  3. **City capacity check** — `assertCityHasCapacity(owner)` (lines 385-397). If city null, returns. Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, excluding self); if `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` (50), throws `CityAtCapacityException(city)`.
  4. **Default registration date** — if null, set to `LocalDate.now()` (server date).
  5. **Roll to business day** — `rollToBusinessDay(...)` (lines 406-418): Saturday → +2 days, Sunday → +1 day, weekday unchanged. Applied to the effective date.
  6. **Daily registration limit** — `assertDailyRegistrationLimit(owner)` (lines 426-438). Counts existing owners with the same `registrationDate` (excluding self); if `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` (100), throws `DailyRegistrationLimitException(registrationDate)`.
  7. **Bulk-signup warning** — `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(computeBulkSignupWarning(owner))` (lines 447-457): true if more than `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (80) owners already share that registration day.
  8. **Customer code** — if new and null, `generateCustomerCode(owner)` (lines 332-341): format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, upper-cased first-3 of city and last name, and a per-city 4-digit sequence = (count of owners already in that city, excluding self) + 1.
  9. **Namesake count** — if new and null, `countNamesakes(owner)` (lines 312-323): count of existing owners (excluding self) with same first+last name (case-insensitive); 0 if either name is null.
  10. **Persist** — `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.
  11. **Audit** — on create, writes one line to the dedicated `"AUDIT"` SLF4J logger with id, customerCode, registrationDate.

  Side-effect / value-assignment constants (lines 58-72): `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50`, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100`, `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80`.

  There is **no password encoding and no email/notification sending** in this path. The only "notification" is the AUDIT log line. All four count-based checks use `ownerRepository.findAll()` and filter in memory.

  The whole method is `@Transactional`, so any thrown exception rolls back.

