        return false;
    }
}
```
Delegates to `Owner.isPostcodeValidForCity` (Owner.java lines 493-506): null/empty postcode is valid; otherwise must be exactly 4 digits; if the city's region (Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD) has a known postcode range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) the value must fall in it; unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode. On failure the violation is re-pointed to the `postcode` field.

(There are also `PetAgeValidation`/`PetAgeValidator` in that package, but they apply to pets, not owners.)

