## End-to-end order of operations (quick reference)
1. Spring Security authorization: `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")`.
2. Jackson deserializes JSON → `OwnerFieldsDto`.
3. `@Valid` bean validation on the DTO: `@NotNull`/`@Size`/`@Pattern`/`@Email` on fields, custom `@TelephoneValidation`, class-level `@PostcodeValidation`. Failures → 400 via `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`.
4. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` → new `Owner` (telephone normalized to E.164 by mapper; address upper-cased/expanded and email lower-cased by entity setters; id/customerCode/namesakeCount left null).
5. `sharesHousehold` read (no-op).
6. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner, sharesHousehold)` inside a transaction: duplicate-telephone check → city-capacity check → default+business-day registration date → daily-limit check → bulk-signup warning → customer code → namesake count → `ownerRepository.save` → AUDIT log.
7. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` builds response with derived fields.
8. `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.
